<OmniUiCard xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <authorName>Diego</authorName>
    <dataSourceConfig>{&quot;dataSource&quot;: {&quot;type&quot;: &quot;Query&quot;, &quot;value&quot;: {&quot;dsDelay&quot;: &quot;&quot;, &quot;query&quot;: &quot;SELECT Id, ServiceResource.Name, ServiceAppointment.AppointmentNumber, ServiceAppointment.Status, ServiceAppointment.SchedStartTime, ServiceAppointment.SchedEndTime, ServiceAppointment.WorkType.Name, ServiceAppointment.ServiceTerritory.Name, ServiceAppointment.Owner.Name, ServiceAppointment.CreatedBy.Name FROM AssignedResource WHERE ServiceResourceId = &#x27;{recordId}&#x27; AND ServiceAppointment.SchedStartTime != NULL ORDER BY ServiceAppointment.SchedStartTime DESC&quot;, &quot;jsonMap&quot;: &quot;{\&quot;recordId\&quot;:\&quot;{recordId}\&quot;}&quot;}, &quot;orderBy&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;&quot;, &quot;isReverse&quot;: &quot;&quot;}, &quot;contextVariables&quot;: [{&quot;name&quot;: &quot;recordId&quot;, &quot;val&quot;: &quot;0Hn000000000000&quot;, &quot;id&quot;: 0}]}}</dataSourceConfig>
    <description>All countries. Agenda of a demo unit for the consultant, placed on the Service Resource record page of the vehicle. Shows every appointment that occupies the unit, test drives and services alike, with date, time, status and the person responsible, and never the customer. The SOQL in the data source is the security control: ServiceAppointment.ParentRecordId is not permissionable, so no field level security can hide the customer, and the only enforceable way is to never select it. Do not add ContactId, ParentRecordId, AccountId, Subject, Description or address fields.</description>
    <isActive>false</isActive>
    <isManagedUsingStdDesigner>true</isManagedUsingStdDesigner>
    <name>DemoVehicleAgenda</name>
    <omniUiCardType>Parent</omniUiCardType>
